1. Executive Overview
1.1 What Leading ITSM Platforms Do
ServiceNow, BMC Remedy, Cherwell, Jira Service Management, and Freshservice implement comprehensive IT Service Management based on ITIL (Information Technology Infrastructure Library) best practices:
* Incident Management - Restore normal service operation as quickly as possible
* Service Request Management - Handle user requests for information, access, or standard changes
* Problem Management - Identify and resolve root causes of recurring incidents
* Change Management - Control the lifecycle of all changes to minimize disruption
* Knowledge Management - Capture, organize, and share information
* Asset Management - Track hardware, software, and configuration items (CIs)
* Service Catalog - User-friendly catalog of available IT services
* SLA Management - Monitor and ensure service level agreements are met
* Self-Service Portal - Enable users to resolve issues and submit requests without agent intervention
1.2 Core Philosophy
Modern ITSM platforms follow these principles:
1. ITIL Alignment - Based on ITIL framework for IT service management
2. Service-Centric - Focus on delivering value through services
3. Automation First - Automate repetitive tasks and workflows
4. Self-Service - Empower users to help themselves
5. Continuous Improvement - Metrics and feedback drive process enhancement
6. Integration - Connect with monitoring, deployment, and business tools
7. Configuration Management - Maintain accurate CMDB for impact analysis
8. Collaboration - Teams work together across departments
