2. Core ITSM Architecture
2.1 Data Model Hierarchy
User (End User)
* Represents people who use IT services
* May submit incidents, requests, and access self-service
* Contains: Name, email, department, location, manager
User Group (Department/Team)
* Logical grouping of users
* Used for routing and permissions
* Contains: Name, manager, members
Assignment Group (Support Team)
* IT support teams that resolve issues
* Examples: Desktop Support, Network Team, Database Admins
* Contains: Name, manager, members, skill sets
Configuration Item (CI)
* Any component that needs to be managed to deliver IT services
* Examples: Servers, applications, network devices, databases
* Relationships between CIs form the CMDB
* Contains: Name, type, status, owner, location, relationships
Service
* IT service offered to users
* Examples: Email Service, VPN Access, Software Development Environment
* Contains: Name, description, owner, SLA, catalog items
Incident
* Unplanned interruption or reduction in quality of service
* Linked to affected user and CI
* Contains: Description, priority, status, assigned group, resolution
Service Request
* User request for information, access, or standard change
* Pre-approved and standardized
* Contains: Type, item requested, approval status, fulfillment tasks
Problem
* Root cause of one or more incidents
* Investigation to prevent future incidents
* Contains: Description, root cause, workaround, related incidents
Change
* Addition, modification, or removal of anything that could affect services
* Follows approval workflow
* Contains: Description, type, risk, implementation plan, approvers
Knowledge Article
* Documented solutions and information
* Searchable by users and agents
* Contains: Title, content, category, tags, attachments
2.2 Relationship Structure
User (End User)
    ↓
Incident / Service Request
    ↓
Assignment Group (Support Team)
    ↓
Resolution / Fulfillment
