6. Change Management
6.1 Change Types
Standard Change:
* Pre-approved, low risk, routine
* Follows established procedure
* Examples: Password reset, add user to group, schedule backup
* Minimal or no approval required
* Can be automated
Normal Change:
* Requires assessment and approval
* Follows standard CAB (Change Advisory Board) process
* Examples: Server patch, application upgrade, network config change
* Risk assessment required
* Implementation plan and backout plan required
Emergency Change:
* Urgent, can't wait for normal process
* Required to fix major incident or security issue
* Expedited approval (Emergency CAB)
* Implemented ASAP
* Retrospective approval possible
6.2 Change Fields
Identification:
* Number (auto-generated: CHG0001234)
* Short Description
* Description (detailed change description)
* Type (Standard, Normal, Emergency)
* Category (Hardware, Software, Network, Security, etc.)
* Configuration Item (what's being changed)
* Service (affected IT service)
Planning:
* Change Requestor (person requesting)
* Assigned To (change coordinator/implementer)
* Implementation Group (team performing change)
* Planned Start Date/Time
* Planned End Date/Time
* Maintenance Window (if during scheduled maintenance)
* Estimated Duration
Risk Assessment:
* Risk (High, Medium, Low)
* Impact (High, Medium, Low - scope of users/systems affected)
* Risk Assessment Notes
* Risk Mitigation Plan
Implementation:
* Implementation Plan (step-by-step instructions)
* Backout Plan (rollback procedure if it fails)
* Testing Plan (how to verify success)
* Change Implementation Notes (log during implementation)
Approval:
* Approval Status (Requested, Approved, Rejected)
* CAB Members (approvers)
* CAB Date (when discussed)
* Approval History
State Workflow:
1. New - Just created
2. Assess - Risk and impact analysis
3. Authorize - Pending CAB approval
4. Scheduled - Approved, scheduled for implementation
5. Implement - Being executed
6. Review - Post-implementation review
7. Closed - Complete and reviewed
Closure:
* Actual Start/End Time
* Change Success (boolean)
* Closure Code (Successful, Successful with Issues, Unsuccessful, Backed Out)
* Closure Notes
* Post-Implementation Review Notes
6.3 Change Advisory Board (CAB)
CAB Membership:
* CAB Chair (Change Manager)
* IT Management representatives
* Application owners
* Infrastructure representatives
* Security representative
* Business representatives
CAB Meeting Cadence:
* Weekly for normal changes
* Daily for emergency changes (as needed)
* Monthly for major changes (requires business approval)
CAB Approval Process:
Change submitted
  ↓
Risk assessment completed
  ↓
Sent to CAB for review
  ↓
CAB discusses in weekly meeting
  ↓
Decision: Approve / Reject / Request More Info
  ↓
If Approved:
  - Schedule for implementation
  - Notify implementer
  - Update change calendar
If Rejected:
  - Notify requestor with reason
  - Close change
If More Info:
  - Return to requestor for additional details
  - Re-submit to next CAB
Emergency CAB (eCAB):
Emergency change created (linked to P1 incident)
  ↓
Notify eCAB members via SMS/email
  ↓
Conference call convened within 30 minutes
  ↓
Quick review (10-15 minutes):
  - What's the issue?
  - What's the proposed change?
  - What's the risk of making the change?
  - What's the risk of NOT making the change?
  - What's the backout plan?
  ↓
Decision: Approve / Reject
  ↓
If Approved: Implement immediately
  ↓
Post-implementation review within 24 hours
6.4 Change Calendar
Calendar Features:
* Visual timeline of all scheduled changes
* Filter by type, category, assignment group
* Conflict detection (multiple changes on same CI)
* Blackout periods (freeze windows - no changes allowed)
* Maintenance windows (pre-approved change windows)
Blackout Periods:
* Financial year-end (no changes 2 weeks before, 1 week after)
* Holiday periods (Thanksgiving week, Christmas/New Year)
* Major business events (annual conference, earnings calls)
* Peak business periods (retail: Black Friday, tax: April)
Change Collision Detection:
IF New change scheduled for CI "Database PROD-SQL-01"
  AND Existing change already scheduled for same CI
  AND Time windows overlap
THEN
  Alert change coordinator: "Conflict detected"
  Require manual review and approval
  Options: Reschedule one change, combine changes, proceed with both
6.5 Change Success Metrics
KPIs Tracked:
* Change Success Rate: (Successful changes / Total changes) × 100%
    * Target: 95%+
* Emergency Change Rate: (Emergency changes / Total changes) × 100%
    * Target: <5%
* Standard Change Automation: Percentage of standard changes fully automated
    * Target: 80%+
* Change-Caused Incidents: Number of incidents caused by failed changes
    * Target: Minimize
* Mean Time to Implement: Average time from approval to completion
    * Target: Within planned duration
Post-Implementation Review:
* Conducted within 48 hours of change completion
* Compare planned vs. actual times
* Document lessons learned
* Update change procedure if needed
* Create knowledge article for successful complex changes

