Event Processing:
1. Event received
2. Normalize (convert to standard format)
3. Correlate (group related events)
4. Deduplicate (filter duplicate events)
5. Enrich (add CI details from CMDB)
6. Apply rules:
   - IF event severity = Critical AND CI = Business Critical
     THEN Create P1 incident
   - IF event matches known error pattern
     THEN Create incident, assign to team, attach KB article
   - IF event = informational
     THEN Log only, don't create incident
7. Create incident (if needed)
8. Close event when incident resolved
Event Correlation:
Events received:
  1. Router CORE-RTR-01: Interface down
  2. Switch FL3-SW-05: Connection lost to router
  3. Server WEB-SVR-12: Network unreachable
  4. Server WEB-SVR-13: Network unreachable
  5. Server WEB-SVR-14: Network unreachable

Correlation:
  Root cause: Router interface down
  Symptoms: All downstream devices lost connectivity
  
Action:
  Create single incident for router (root cause)
  Link all other events as related
  Don't create separate incidents for each server
  
Incident:
  INC0012347 - Router CORE-RTR-01 interface down
  Impact: 3 web servers unreachable
  Priority: P1 (Business Critical CI)
